#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:398
msgid "Formats to generate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:399
msgid "AVIF files are smaller than WebP but take longer to encode and are understood by slightly fewer browsers. Generating both lets each visitor receive the smallest file their browser can read. Formats your server cannot encode are listed as unavailable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:406
msgid "Convert new uploads"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:407
msgid "Generate the optimized copies as soon as an image is uploaded or its thumbnails are regenerated."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:413
msgid "Image sizes to convert"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:414
msgid "Leave every box unchecked to convert all sizes, which is what you want unless disk space is tight. A responsive image only switches format when every size in its srcset has been converted, so excluding a size that appears in your themes markup disables the optimization for those images."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:421
msgid "Minimum saving (%)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:422
msgid "Discard an optimized copy unless it is at least this much smaller than the original. Small or already-compressed images frequently grow when re-encoded, and keeping those wastes disk space for no benefit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:431
msgid "Optimized file naming"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:432
msgid "Append keeps the original extension and adds the new one, e.g. photo.jpg.webp — this is the safe default. Replace produces photo.webp instead, but if a folder ever contains both photo.jpg and photo.png, their optimized copies would collide on the same photo.webp file and one would silently overwrite the other. Only choose Replace if you are sure your uploads never share a filename across extensions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:436
msgid "Append the new extension (photo.jpg.webp) — safe"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:437
msgid "Replace the extension (photo.webp) — can collide"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:457
msgid "WebP quality"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:458
msgid "Between 1 and 100. The default of 82 is visually indistinguishable from the original for most photographs. Values above 90 grow the file quickly for very little visible gain."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:467
msgid "AVIF quality"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:468
msgid "Between 1 and 100. AVIF and WebP quality numbers are not comparable: AVIF at 50 looks about the same as WebP at 82 while producing a noticeably smaller file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:477
msgid "WebP encoder effort"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:478
msgid "Between 0 and 6. Higher values spend more CPU time searching for a smaller file at identical visual quality. Because conversion happens once and the result is served many times, the highest setting is usually the right trade. Lower it if bulk runs are timing out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:487
msgid "AVIF encoder effort"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:488
msgid "Between 0 and 6. AVIF encoding is much slower than WebP, so the default is lower. The plugin also automatically speeds up encoding for very large images where the quality gain per pixel is small. Raise this for smaller files at the cost of longer conversion times."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:497
msgid "Strip metadata"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:498
msgid "Remove EXIF, GPS and embedded thumbnails from the optimized copies. The colour profile is always kept, so colours will not shift. Your original files are never modified."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:504
msgid "Lossless for PNG sources"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:505
msgid "Encode PNG sources without any quality loss. This is the right choice for logos, screenshots and line art, but produces much larger files for photographs saved as PNG."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:526
msgid "Serve optimized images"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:527
msgid "Wrap images in a picture element so the browser picks the best format it supports. Because the choice is made by the browser rather than the server, this works correctly behind page caches and CDNs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:533
msgid "Post content images"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:534
msgid "Rewrite images embedded in post and page content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:540
msgid "Theme and block images"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:541
msgid "Rewrite featured images, gallery images and any image rendered by a theme or block through the WordPress image functions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:547
msgid "Whole page (buffered)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:549
msgid "Catch images printed directly by a page builder or a hard-coded template by rewriting the whole page through the WordPress template enhancement output buffer. This catches the most images but costs a little memory on every request, so leave it off unless you can see images the two options above are missing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:550
msgid "Requires WordPress 6.9 or later, which provides the template enhancement output buffer this option uses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:557
msgid "CSS background images"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:578
msgid "Images per batch"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:579
msgid "How many attachments to process in a single bulk step. Lower this if your server times out during a bulk run; raise it to finish faster on a fast server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:588
msgid "Process the queue in the background"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:589
msgid "Keep working through the queue on a schedule even when the bulk screen is closed. Turn this off if you would rather the queue only advance while you watch it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:595
msgid "Queue images on first view"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:596
msgid "When a page references an image that has not been converted yet, serve the original immediately and add the image to the queue. Nothing is ever converted during a page render, so visitors never wait for an encode."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:602
msgid "Exclude paths"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:603
msgid "One fragment per line. Any image whose path inside the uploads folder contains one of these fragments is left alone, for example 2019/07 or /logos/."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:609
msgid "Delete optimized files on uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:610
msgid "Remove every generated WebP and AVIF file when the plugin is deleted. Your original images are never touched either way. Leave this off if you may reinstall later and would rather not convert everything again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:616
msgid "Delete settings and records on uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-settings.php:617
msgid "Remove the settings, the queue table and the per-image conversion records when the plugin is deleted."
msgstr ""

